    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nsetup osc52 clipboard take 2 line\n```\n-- init.lua\nvim.o.clipboard = \"unnamedplus\"\nvim.g.clipboard = \"osc52\" -- only works before calling vim.fn[\"has\"](\"clipboard\")\n```\nhow ever this is quite flaw as it is always enabled. There for, cant paste due to security reason\n```\nvim.o.clipboard = \"unnamedplus\"\nif vim.fn[\"has\"](\"clipboard\") == 0 then\n  vim.g.clipboard = \"osc52\"\nelse\n  vim.g.clipboard = \"unnameplus\"\n\n[nvim-osc52-bug.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/30380990/nvim-osc52-bug.zip)\n\nend\n```\nsome bug(I think) stop\nsetting vim.g.clipboard to works after calling ```vim.fn[\"has\"](\"clipboard\")```\n\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- download the docker build instruction   \n- add your ssh pupkey to authorized_keys\n  - replace wl-paste with yourown in ./build_run.fish\n- Makesure youare running the ./build_run.fish script in a terminal, nvim terminal is fine\n- You can also test vim however you have to type yy:wq<enter> manualy because vim run cmd before open interactive mode\n\n### Expected behavior\n\n  - check clipboard or the result\n  - or the stdout\n  ```\n    Shared connection to localhost closed.\n    111111111111111\n    Shared connection to localhost closed.\n    222222222222222\n  ```\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nNVIM v0.12.4\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nno, vim 9.2.0735-1\n\n### Operating system/version\n\narchlinux:base-20260712.0.555161\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nnvim terminal in side docker|| kitty : 0.48.0-1\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nxterm-kitty\n\n### Installation\n\npacman",
